 75GA    76GE(D,3HE),(POL D,3HE)       1978RO14,2009KA06         13NDS    201309
 75GA  H TYP=FUL$AUT=ALEXANDRU NEGRET, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 114, 841 (2013)$    
 75GA2 H CUT=30-Jun-2013$                                                       
 75GA c  The (pol d, {+3}He) data are from 2009Ka06                             
 75GA c  1978Ro14: E=26 MeV, 1|mA deuterium beam accelerated by the Orsay MP    
 75GA2c  tandem accelerator, a GeO{-2} target (enrichment 95.5% in {+76}Ge,     
 75GA3c  thickness 67 |mg/cm{+2}). A split pole magnetic spectrometer was used  
 75GA4c  with four solid state position sensitive detectors in the focal plane. 
 75GA5c  FWHM=15 keV for the {+3}He spectra. Measured |s(|q) with an            
 75GA6c  absolute uncertainty of the order of 20%. DWBA calculations performed  
 75GA7c  with the DWUCK code.                                                   
 75GA c  2009Ka06, 2008KaZT: E=80 MeV beam provided by the AVF cyclotron        
 75GA2c  at RCNP, Osaka. Enriched target. Vector-polarized 80 MeV deuteron beam 
 75GA3c  with A{-y}=0.520 {I10}, {+3}He outgoing particles detected and analyzed
 75GA4c  with the Grand Raiden magnetic spectrometer, with an angular aperture  
 75GA5c  of |+1.1|'. FWHM=50 keV. Measured precise absolute cross sections and  
 75GA6c  relative cross sections where these are maximum for the relevant L     
 75GA7c  transfer, angular distributions and polarization asymmetries. Vector   
 75GA8c  analyzing powers were deduced from the measured polarization           
 75GA9c  asymmetries by dividing by a factor of 1.04 (2*[beam vector            
 75GAac  polarization=0.520 {I10}]). Spectroscopic factors were deduced from    
 75GAbc  analysis of cross section data by DWBA calculations using PTOLEMY code 
 75GAcc  and six different sets of optical-model potential parameters and two   
 75GAdc  bound-state potential parameters. The polarized deuteron beam is also  
 75GAec  used to obtain asymmetries and subsequent information about parities   
 75GAfc  of levels.                                                             
 75GA c  Other: 1984Ha31: E=21-24 MeV; measured mass excess                     
